    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.346 ALMA-09-045125"
      info        : "AlmaLinux OS 9 must be a supported release.

GROUP ID: V-269454
RULE ID: SV-269454r1184107

Security flaws with operating systems are discovered daily. Vendors are constantly updating and patching their products to address newly discovered security vulnerabilities. Organizations (including any contractor to the organization) are required to promptly install security-relevant software updates (e.g., patches, service packs, and hot fixes). Flaws discovered during security assessments, continuous monitoring, incident response activities, or information system error handling must also be addressed expeditiously.

End Of Life dates for AlmaLinux OS 9 releases are as follows:
Active/Full Support: 31 May 2027.
Security only/Maintenance Support: 31 May 2032.

NOTE: Nessus has provided the target output to assist in reviewing the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "Extended vendor support is available from TuxCare as part of the Enterprise Support for AlmaLinux product line. Access this (and the FIPS packages) by purchasing an ESU license key."
      reference   : "800-171|3.14.1,800-171r3|03.14.01b.,800-53|SI-2c.,800-53r5|SI-2c.,CCI|CCI-002605,CN-L3|8.1.4.4(e),CN-L3|8.1.10.5(a),CN-L3|8.1.10.5(b),CN-L3|8.5.4.1(b),CN-L3|8.5.4.1(d),CN-L3|8.5.4.1(e),CSF|ID.RA-1,CSF|PR.IP-12,CSF2.0|ID.IM-01,CSF2.0|ID.IM-02,CSF2.0|ID.IM-03,CSF2.0|PR.PS-02,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.6.8,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.8,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.32,ITSG-33|SI-2,LEVEL|1M,NESA|T7.6.2,NESA|T7.7.1,NIAv2|AM38,NIAv2|AM39,NIAv2|SS14b,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|6.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|6.3,PCI-DSSv4.0|6.3.3,QCSC-v1|11.2,Rule-ID|SV-269454r1184107_rule,STIG-ID|ALMA-09-045125,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.2,Vuln-ID|V-269454"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27039"
      file        : "/etc/almalinux-release"
      regex       : ".*"
      expect      : "^Manual Review Required$"
      severity    : MEDIUM
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.36 ALMA-09-006620"
      info        : "The systemd Ctrl-Alt-Delete burst key sequence in AlmaLinux OS 9 must be disabled.

GROUP ID: V-269140
RULE ID: SV-269140r1050022

A locally logged-on user who presses Ctrl-Alt-Delete in quick succession when at the console can reboot the system.

If accidentally pressed, as could happen in the case of a mixed OS environment, this can create the risk of short-term loss of availability of systems due to unintentional reboot.

In a graphical user environment, risk of unintentional reboot from the Ctrl-Alt-Delete sequence is reduced because the user will be prompted before any action is taken."
      solution    : "Configure the system to disable the CtrlAltDelBurstAction by added or modifying the following line in the \"/etc/systemd/system.conf\" configuration file:

CtrlAltDelBurstAction=none

Reload the daemon for this change to take effect.

$ systemctl daemon-reexec"
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.7,800-171r3|03.01.07a.,800-53|AC-6(10),800-53r5|AC-6(10),CCI|CCI-002235,CN-L3|7.1.3.2(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.2(g),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(d),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(a),CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ITSG-33|AC-6,LEVEL|1A,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.2.2,NESA|T5.4.1,NESA|T5.4.4,NESA|T5.4.5,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM1,NIAv2|AM23f,NIAv2|SS13c,NIAv2|SS15c,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|7.1.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,Rule-ID|SV-269140r1050022_rule,STIG-ID|ALMA-09-006620,SWIFT-CSCv1|5.1,TBA-FIISB|31.4.2,TBA-FIISB|31.4.3,Vuln-ID|V-269140"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27039"
      file        : "/etc/systemd/system.conf"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*CtrlAltDelBurstAction[\\s]*="
      expect      : "^[\\s]*CtrlAltDelBurstAction[\\s]*=[\\s]*none"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.39 ALMA-09-006730"
      info        : "The Ctrl-Alt-Delete key sequence must be disabled on AlmaLinux OS 9.

GROUP ID: V-269141
RULE ID: SV-269141r1101851

A locally logged-on user who presses Ctrl-Alt-Delete when at the console can reboot the system.

If accidentally pressed, as could happen in the case of a mixed OS environment, this can create the risk of short-term loss of availability of systems due to unintentional reboot.

In a graphical user environment, risk of unintentional reboot from the Ctrl-Alt-Delete sequence is reduced because the user will be prompted before any action is taken."
      solution    : "Configure AlmaLinux OS 9 to disable the ctrl-alt-del.target with the following command:

$ systemctl disable --now ctrl-alt-del.target

$ systemctl mask --now ctrl-alt-del.target"
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.7,800-171r3|03.01.07a.,800-53|AC-6(10),800-53r5|AC-6(10),CCI|CCI-002235,CN-L3|7.1.3.2(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.2(g),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(d),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(a),CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ITSG-33|AC-6,LEVEL|1A,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.2.2,NESA|T5.4.1,NESA|T5.4.4,NESA|T5.4.5,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM1,NIAv2|AM23f,NIAv2|SS13c,NIAv2|SS15c,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|7.1.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,Rule-ID|SV-269141r1101851_rule,STIG-ID|ALMA-09-006730,SWIFT-CSCv1|5.1,TBA-FIISB|31.4.2,TBA-FIISB|31.4.3,Vuln-ID|V-269141"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27039"
      cmd         : "/bin/systemctl status ctrl-alt-del.target | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"No results found\"'}"
      expect      : "(^[\\s]*Loaded:[\\s]*[Mm]asked|No results found)"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.60 ALMA-09-009590"
      info        : "AlmaLinux OS 9 must check the GPG signature of software packages originating from external software repositories before installation.

GROUP ID: V-269163
RULE ID: SV-269163r1050045

Changes to any software components can have significant effects on the overall security of the operating system. This requirement ensures the software has not been tampered with and that it has been provided by a trusted vendor.

Accordingly, patches, service packs, device drivers, or operating system components must be signed with a certificate recognized and approved by the organization.

Verifying the authenticity of the software prior to installation validates the integrity of the patch or upgrade received from a vendor. This ensures the software has not been tampered with and that it has been provided by a trusted vendor. Self-signed certificates are not allowed by this requirement. The operating system should not have to verify the software again. This requirement does not mandate DOD certificates for this purpose; however, the certificate used to verify the software must be from an approved certificate authority (CA)."
      solution    : "Configure dnf to always check the GPG signature of software packages originating from external software repositories before installation.

Add or update the following line in the [main] section of the /etc/dnf/dnf.conf file:

gpgcheck=1"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.5,800-171r3|03.04.05,800-53|CM-5(3),800-53r5|CM-14,CCI|CCI-003992,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.4,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.19,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.31,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.32,ITSG-33|CM-5(3),LEVEL|1A,NESA|T3.2.3,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.1,NESA|T7.5.3,NESA|T7.6.3,QCSC-v1|7.2,Rule-ID|SV-269163r1050045_rule,STIG-ID|ALMA-09-009590,Vuln-ID|V-269163"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27039"
      file        : "/etc/dnf/dnf.conf"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*gpgcheck[\\s]*="
      expect      : "^[\\s]*gpgcheck[\\s]*=[\\s]*1[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "TuxCare key"
          cmd         : "/bin/rpm rpm -q --queryformat \"%{SUMMARY}\\n\" gpg-pubkey"
          expect      : "[\\s]*TuxCare[\\s]+\\(Software[\\s]+Signing[\\s]+Key\\)[\\s]+(<packager@tuxcare\\.com>[\\s]+)?public[\\s]+key[\\s]*"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "AlmaLinux key"
          cmd         : "/bin/rpm rpm -q --queryformat \"%{SUMMARY}\\n\" gpg-pubkey"
          expect      : "[\\s]*AlmaLinux[\\s]+OS[\\s]+9[\\s]+(<packager@almalinux\\.org>[\\s]+)?public[\\s]+key[\\s]*"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "TuxCare fingerprint"
          cmd         : "/bin/gpg -q --keyid-format short --with-fingerprint /etc/pki/rpm-gpg/RPM-GPG-KEY-AlmaLinux-9"
          expect      : "^(?i)[\\s]*Key[\\s]+fingerprint[\\s]*=[\\s]*BF18[\\s]*AC28[\\s]*7617[\\s]*8908[\\s]*D6E7[\\s]*1267[\\s]*D36C[\\s]*B86C[\\s]*B86B[\\s]*3716$"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "AlmaLinux fingerprint"
          cmd         : "/bin/gpg -q --keyid-format short --with-fingerprint /etc/pki/rpm-gpg/RPM-GPG-KEY-TuxCare"
          expect      : "^(?i)[\\s]*Key[\\s]+fingerprint[\\s]*=[\\s]*FAD7[\\s]*8590[\\s]*81D0[\\s]*738B[\\s]*7A82[\\s]*8496[\\s]*D07B[\\s]*F2A0[\\s]*8D50[\\s]*EB66$"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.61 ALMA-09-009700"
          info        : "AlmaLinux OS 9 must ensure cryptographic verification of vendor software packages.

GROUP ID: V-269164
RULE ID: SV-269164r1050046

Changes to any software components can have significant effects on the overall security of the operating system. This requirement ensures the software has not been tampered with and that it has been provided by a trusted vendor.

Accordingly, patches, service packs, device drivers, or operating system components must be signed with a certificate recognized and approved by the organization.

Verifying the authenticity of the software prior to installation validates the integrity of the patch or upgrade received from a vendor. This ensures the software has not been tampered with and that it has been provided by a trusted vendor. Self-signed certificates are not allowed by this requirement. The operating system should not have to verify the software again. This requirement does not mandate DOD certificates for this purpose; however, the certificate used to verify the software must be from an approved certificate authority (CA)."
          solution    : "Install AlmaLinux and TuxCare package-signing keys on the system and verify their fingerprints match vendor values.

$ curl https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/RPM-GPG-KEY-AlmaLinux-9 -o /etc/pki/rpm-gpg/RPM-GPG-KEY-AlmaLinux-9

$ curl https://repo.tuxcare.com/tuxcare/RPM-GPG-KEY-TuxCare -o /etc/pki/rpm-gpg/RPM-GPG-KEY-TuxCare

$ rpm --import https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/RPM-GPG-KEY-AlmaLinux-9

$ rpm --import https://repo.tuxcare.com/tuxcare/RPM-GPG-KEY-TuxCare

Using the steps listed in the Check, confirm the newly imported keys show as installed on the system and verify their fingerprints match vendor values."
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.5,800-171r3|03.04.05,800-53|CM-5(3),800-53r5|CM-14,CCI|CCI-003992,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.4,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.19,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.31,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.32,ITSG-33|CM-5(3),LEVEL|1M,NESA|T3.2.3,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.1,NESA|T7.5.3,NESA|T7.6.3,QCSC-v1|7.2,Rule-ID|SV-269164r1050046_rule,STIG-ID|ALMA-09-009700,Vuln-ID|V-269164"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/27039"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>
    </if>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.62 ALMA-09-009810"
      info        : "AlmaLinux OS 9 must check the GPG signature of locally installed software packages before installation.

GROUP ID: V-269165
